  {
    "sha": "6c540c0493cc859aaca66c5163ffbbee7d5a59fa",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOT6BV9NoAKDZjNTQwYzA0OTNjYzg1OWFhY2E2NmM1MTYzZmZiYmVlN2Q1YTU5ZmE",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Schum",
        "email": "sergey@kivaev.ru",
        "date": "2026-10-17T05:22:41Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Schum",
        "email": "sergey@kivaev.ru",
        "date": "2026-10-17T05:22:52Z"
      },
      "message": "genesis-block-wallet-puzzle: SOLVED by Schum-io on 2026-10-17, folder moved to 4-solved\n\nBoth cosigners come from one 12-word mnemonic whose entropy is the first 128 bits of\nsha256 of the coinbase text's hex (cut -b 263-400 of the raw block hex), passphrase\nSatoshi Nakamoto, PBKDF2 at 181505 (18:15:05) and 200913 (2009/1/3) rounds, both keys at\nm/48'/0'/1231006505'/2'/0/0. The escrow (946,540 sats, 117 outputs) was swept in block\n971803, 935,266 sats to the solver; the author acknowledged the solve on chain.\n\n- README: SOLVED badge, the post-September author answers, mechanism, Solution section\n- puzzle.json: tier/status solved, prize and address state, solutions[], leads closed\n- clues/author-posts.md and data/on-chain-dialogue.json: 95 new transactions (119 total)\n- analysis/tested.md and leads.md: closed by the solve, all negatives were at 2048 rounds\n- tools/verify_solution.py: rebuilds both keys from data/genesis-block.hex, oracle MATCH AB\n- puzzles.json and the generated README tables regenerated\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
